Installing imud
===============

Prerequisites (Raspberry Pi OS / Debian trixie, Bookworm, or similar):

    sudo apt install build-essential libgpiod-dev

Build and install the core — the imud daemon plus imud-cal, imud-status,
the client libraries, the config, the systemd unit, and man pages — and the
World Magnetic Model data (needed for true-heading output):

    make
    sudo make install
    sudo make install-wmm-data

Installs to /usr/local by default. Override the prefix, or stage into a
packaging root, with the standard variables:

    sudo make install PREFIX=/usr
    make install DESTDIR=/tmp/stage PREFIX=/usr        # staged, no root needed

Packaging notes: when DESTDIR is set the install is a pure file copy — no
system user is created and systemctl/ldconfig are never invoked (those belong
to a package's maintainer scripts). Packagers should also set
SVCDIR=/lib/systemd/system (systemd units are generated from
etc/*.service.in with the chosen bin dir), and CC/CFLAGS/CPPFLAGS/LDFLAGS
from the environment (e.g. dpkg-buildflags) are respected. `make dist`
produces the upstream release tarball from git HEAD. See packaging/README.

Client development: `make install` ships libimud (libimud.so.0 + imud.h +
pkg-config metadata). Third-party apps build with

    cc app.c $(pkg-config --cflags --libs libimud)

and stay binary-compatible across imud upgrades (see man 3 libimud). The
bridges link libimud themselves; when running them from the build tree on
Linux (not installed), prefix LD_LIBRARY_PATH=. so they find the freshly
built library.

Optional bridge daemons are built and installed separately — each is its own
package with its own dependencies, config, and docs:

    make bridges                                       # build all bridges
    sudo make install-signalk                          # Signal K bridge
    sudo make install-mqtt                             # MQTT bridge (needs libmosquitto-dev)
    sudo make install-influxdb                         # InfluxDB bridge
    sudo make install-mavlink                          # MAVLink bridge
    sudo make install-prometheus                       # Prometheus exporter
    sudo make install-utils                            # imud-mon network monitor

Prebuilt arm64 .debs for Debian/Raspberry Pi OS bookworm and trixie are
attached to GitHub releases (https://github.com/richcreations/imud/releases):
imud, imud-utils, libimud0, libimud-dev, the five bridges, and imud-wmm-data.

Edit the configuration for your hardware, then enable the service:

    sudo nano /etc/imud/imud.conf
    sudo systemctl enable --now imud

Other targets:

    make test            # run the test suite (from the repo root)
    sudo make uninstall  # remove installed files (config in /etc/imud is kept)

The full installation, configuration, and calibration guide is docs/manual.md
(installed to /usr/share/doc/imud/manual.md).
